From 7cd9610894544be50e56c7d79be7ac29e1988abd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <a@b>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:12:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 1006 vince: vincemdptest maps less I/O space so the GPU
 bring-up still fits

The test mapped 7.3 MiB of the 8 MiB I/O submap and never gave it back, so the next
kmem_alloc of 384 KiB in adreno step 1 failed with KERN_NO_SPACE and panicked. Map only the
control blocks it uses and 1 MiB of the second buffer (the top of the screen shows the colour).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UTtYRgmKyxgNh36HwFrzar
---
 bsd/dev/vince_adreno.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bsd/dev/vince_adreno.c b/bsd/dev/vince_adreno.c
index dc49394..e75c8b1 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/vince_adreno.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/vince_adreno.c
@@ -1088,8 +1088,12 @@ vince_mdp_dump(void)
 static void
 vince_mdp_flip_test(void)
 {
-	const uint32_t buf0 = 0x90001000, buf1 = 0x90801000, size = 0x6ac000;
-	vm_offset_t mdp = ml_io_map(0x01a01000, 0x6c000);
+	/*
+	 * The I/O submap is only 8 MiB and mappings are never released, so map as little as possible: the control
+	 * blocks up to CTL4 (0x16000) and 1 MiB of the second buffer (about a seventh of the screen, from the top).
+	 */
+	const uint32_t buf0 = 0x90001000, buf1 = 0x90801000, size = 0x100000;
+	vm_offset_t mdp = ml_io_map(0x01a01000, 0x16000);
 	vm_offset_t fb = ml_io_map_wcomb(buf1, size);
 	volatile uint32_t *src0;
 	uint32_t c, i, t;
-- 
